  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to have a target relationship with the putative FAD-monooxygenase through multiple pathways, with the highest confidence scores in path_152701 and path_152702. These pathways indicate that Oblonganoside C acts as a modulator of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets the putative FAD-monooxygenase. The shared involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol across these paths suggests a potential central role in the observed interactions, though the exact mechanism of Ent-Gloeosteretriol's interaction with the FAD-monooxygenase remains unclear. The presence of multiple targets (ICK, GSK-3α) further supports a complex regulatory network, but the core mechanism linking Oblonganoside C to the FAD-monooxygenase is not fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a functional relationship, but the precise molecular pathways and the role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol require further investigation to establish a robust mechanistic link.",
